-=> 2) When playing, H's from the "cm"-termcap-entry keep appearing on the
-=>    screen. Looks awful. Why ?

Because Fish's termcap library has a bug.  You can ftp a bugfixed
version from linc.cis.upenn.edu's /pub/NH3.0 directory as anonymous.

-=> 3) WHY DOESN'T THE KEYS HAVE THEIR USUAL PLACE (grrr....)
-=>    Is there somewhere where the cursor-arrows can be switched off, or
-=>    is it some kinda option ???

I assume you mean you want to use [yuhjklbn] to move.  NetHack 3.0 has
a number_pad option (default off) that makes the number keys move
instead of [yuhjklbn].  Remove "number_pad" from the OPTIONS line in
NetHack.cnf.

If you really want to turn off the cursor keys as well (and the
Alt-letter handling and fast video updates), remove "IBM_BIOS" from the
OPTIONS line in NetHack.cnf.

Speaking of Alt-letter handling, Timo sent us a fix for foreign
keyboards that will be in Patch4.


